{"content":{"result":[{"rank_order":1,"title":"IAM roles last used and last accessed information available in AWS GovCloud (US) Regions","context":"The AWS documentation announces the availability of IAM roles last used and last accessed information in AWS GovCloud (US) Regions. This feature allows users to identify and remove unused roles by reporting the latest timestamp when role credentials were used to make an AWS request. Additionally, the latest timestamp when an IAM user or role used an action is provided, enabling users to refine access for their workloads by identifying unused service and action-level permissions","url":"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/whats-new/2023/09/iam-roles-last-used-accessed-information-aws-govcloud-regions/"},{"rank_order":2,"title":"AWS Service Reference Information now supports actions for last accessed services - AWS","context":"AWS has updated its service reference information to include details about the actions supported by the IAM Last Accessed and IAM Access Analyzer Policy Generation features. These features assist in achieving least privilege permissions. The new service reference information can be automatically retrieved, reducing manual effort and ensuring alignment with the latest service updates. Users can incorporate this information into their policy management tools and processes for seamless integration. The feature comes at no additional cost. To get started, refer to the programmatic service reference information documentation","url":"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/whats-new/2025/07/aws-service-reference-information-actions-last-accessed-services/"},{"rank_order":3,"title":"setting-up-cloudtrail-multi-region","skill_description":"Enables a multi-region AWS CloudTrail trail with S3 log storage, CloudWatch Logs integration, and CloudWatch Logs Insights queries for security monitoring and compliance auditing. Use when setting up centralized API activity logging across all AWS regions.\n\nServices: cloudtrail, s3, cloudwatch, iam, kms\nTasks: configure, secure, monitor\nPersona: developer, devops\nWorkload: security, monitoring\n*","skill_name":"setting-up-cloudtrail-multi-region"},{"rank_order":4,"title":"aws-investigation","skill_description":"Investigates what is happening in an AWS account from evidence already recorded there. Not for capturing new data from running code (snapshots of function arguments on a live service, Dynamic Instrumentation), questions answered from the CloudWatch Omni context graph or Application Signals service map, or building or changing infrastructure. Covers reading deployment records instead of the newest stored version (completed AppConfig deployments, the version an alias points to, a stack's current template), following a request through every service's own logs (exact per-layer fields, unique failed requests in an alarm's breach window, failure boundary per event), and answering questions from the account's data (exact counts and breakdowns, coverage of the requested range, exact filters and joins, the rule behind failed or unmatched records, verbatim values). Use to triage an alarm, error spike or failed request, trace a request across services, or count, break down, extract or join records.\n\nServices: cloudwatch, appconfig, lambda, cloudformation, dynamodb, s3, athena, glue\nTasks: debug, investigate, query, troubleshoot\nPersona: developer, devops\nWorkload: observability, operations","skill_name":"aws-investigation"},{"rank_order":5,"title":"querying-aws-cloudwatch","skill_description":"Runs SQL queries on CloudWatch Logs data exported as Apache Iceberg tables in S3 Tables. Covers VPC Flow Logs, WAF logs, CloudFront access logs, Route 53 resolver logs, Network Firewall logs, EKS audit logs, Verified Access logs, SES logs, VPC Lattice logs, Step Functions logs, NLB access logs, S3 Server Access Logs, and 20+ other AWS vended data sources. Applies when analyzing network traffic, investigating security incidents, querying exported logs with SQL, enabling S3 Tables integration, configuring log export, correlating logs with other data, running Athena queries on the aws-cloudwatch table bucket, analyzing S3 access patterns, S3 latency investigation, S3 cost attribution, or bucket access auditing.\n\nServices: cloudwatch, s3tables, athena, glue, s3\nTasks: build, deploy, debug, audit, configure\nPersona: developer, data-engineer, devops\nWorkload: data-analytics, observability\n*","skill_name":"querying-aws-cloudwatch"}]}}"}]}], "label": "Verify IAM role last-used/Access Advisor capability for checking role usage"}
